From: mscharged-port
Subject: Tweak: a replay poses its characters on more threads
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

A step poses the ten characters in cCharacter::PostPhysicsUpdate, one after
the other: cPoseAccumulator::Pose evaluates the animation tree (about a
fifth of a step), then builds the bone matrices. The evaluation reads only
the character's own tree, animations and accumulator.

While a replay plays (a spectator catching up most of all), PhysicsUpdate
now begins by having the port copy the ten trees and accumulators and
evaluate the copies on the host's worker threads while the collisions and
the physics engine's step run (parallel_pose.cpp); it waits for them after
the step. PostPhysicsUpdate takes a character's result only if everything
its evaluation read is still the same, and then builds the bone matrices as
before, in the same order (their callbacks read the other characters and
the ball); else it poses as before. The same calculations on the same
inputs: the match plays exactly as it would, and a match that is not a
replay never asks.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_replay.h b/include/mscharged_replay.h
index 2730d2b..12e2852 100644
--- a/include/mscharged_replay.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_replay.h
@@ -57,6 +57,16 @@ bool mscharged_tweak_replay_turbo(void);
 // 10 s. Nothing in the match reads them, only the goal replays and the
 // drawing, which the screen hides.
 bool mscharged_tweak_replay_skips_snapshot(void);
+// Parallel posing while a replay plays (tweak patch 0091, the port's
+// parallel_pose.cpp): PhysicsUpdate begins by having the characters' poses
+// evaluated on other threads (from copies of their trees), and waits for
+// them after the physics engine's step; cCharacter::PostPhysicsUpdate then
+// takes its pose's evaluation (`accumulator` posed with `tree`) when
+// everything it read is unchanged, and only builds the bone matrices, or
+// poses as before when it is not taken.
+void mscharged_tweak_pose_begin(void);
+void mscharged_tweak_pose_end(void);
+bool mscharged_tweak_pose_take(void* accumulator, const void* tree);
 // How many times faster the wipes around cutscenes run: more than 1 while a
 // live replay catches up.
 float mscharged_tweak_replay_wipe_speed(void);
